  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Akhtar Beg Ayyub Beg vs The State Of Maharashtra on 15 July, 2021 Author: Bharati Dangre Bench: Bharati Dangre 1/3 19 ABA-1566-21.doc In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Anticipatory Bail Application No.1566 Of 2021 Akhtar Beg Ayyub Beg .. Applicant Versus The State of Maharashtra .. Respondent ... Mr.Milind Deshmukh for the Applicant. Mr.Y.M.Nakhava, APP for the State. ... CORAM: BHARATI DANGRE, J. DATED : 15th JULY, 2021 P.C:- 1. C.R.No.623 of 2021 is registered with Sangola Police Station invoking Sections 188, 272, 273, 328 read with Section 34 of the IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "The allegation in the complaint is to the effect that one truck loaded with Hira Pan Masala and Royal 717 tobacco was being plied on 25/05/2021 in the jurisdiction of the complainant and the said truck was brought to the police station. The driver of the truck revealed that the material in the said truck was purchased from Raibaug, Dist. Belgaum, Karnataka and it was being transported to Aurangabad and was meant for one Attar Haji i.e. the present applicant. Learned counsel for the applicant states that the driver and the cleaner of the truck are released on bail by the Additional Sessions Judge, Pandharpur. Further, the complaint also allege that it was a prohibited substance and the description of the said substance with its quantity is specifed in the complaint itself. On the last date of hearing, learned APP has pointed out that there are four CRs registered against the present applicant, which indicated his involvement in the prohibited M.M.Salgaonkar 2/3 22 ABA-1566-21.doc substance. The CRs are of recent time which indicate that the applicant is involved constantly in the said activity of bringing the prohibited substance in the State of Maharashtra, as per the direction of the Commissioner of Food Safety vide the relevant notifcations issued and he is habituated of selling the said material in the State of Maharashtra. 3. Today, the learned APP has also placed on record the details of four CRs against the present Akhtar Beg Ayyub Beg vs The State Of Maharashtra on 26 August, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/164424070/ 1 applicant, which are as under :- 1) FIR No.139 of 2020 registered with Phulambri Police Station, Aurangabad Gramin for the offences punishable under Sections 188, 273 read with 34 of IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006; 2) FIR No.247 of 2019 registered with Phulambri Police Station, Aurangabad Gramin for the offences punishable under Sections 272, 273 of IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006; 3) FIR No.223 of 2020 registered with Daulatabad Police Station, District Aurangabad for the offences punishable under Sections 307, 353, 328, 188, 273, 279, 427, 109, 114, 120-B read with Section 34 of IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006; 4) FIR No.164 of 2020 registered with Bhokardan Police Station, District Jalna for the offences punishable under Sections 143, 147, 149, 323, 504, 506 of IPC. Learned APP has also placed on record a charge-sheet fled in C.R.No.223 of 2020 where the applicant is charged with bringing the prohibited substance from Karnataka in the State of Maharashtra and indulging into a conspiracy with the other accused persons in selling the said prohibited substance. On noting that one offence is of the year 2019 and three other offences registered in District Aurangabad and Jalna pertain to the 2020, reveal the continuous activity of the applicant in bringing the prohibited substance in the State of Maharashtra and fruther dealing in the same.",
    "arguments": "(c) The applicant shall not directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with facts of case so as to dissuade him from disclosing the facts to Court or any Police Offcer and shall not tamper with the prosecution evidence.",
